Third-Party Software Notices
============================

This project ships with, downloads, or calls the third-party work listed here.
Each entry gives the licence it is distributed under and where it comes from.
The Python section is generated (`make notices`); everything else is kept by
hand. The project itself is MIT (see LICENSE).

Cut review frontend
-------------------

The Python package includes the Svelte contact sheet built from frontend/.
Its bundled dependency licences are generated by Vite and shipped alongside it
in src/immich_memories/ui/static/review/licenses.md (also /static/review/licenses.md
in the running app). The exact build dependencies are pinned in frontend/package-lock.json.


Models (bundled, or downloaded by `immich-memories models fetch`, digest-pinned)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DINOv2 small (facebook/dinov2-small)
  Role: the frozen picture encoder every editorial fact is computed from
  Artifact: dinov2-small-478164cd.onnx, an ONNX export of the checkpoint,
    served from this repository's `models-v1` release, 84 MB,
    sha256 478164cd290ee78e5ddb4fcc474136eec714b4b8253a3609cc7164b592e958af
  License: Apache-2.0
  Copyright: Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates
  URL: https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov2-small
  Paper: Oquab et al., "DINOv2: Learning Robust Visual Features without
    Supervision", 2023
  Note: the eight linear heads that read its features are trained by this project
    and ship inside the Python package under the project licence.

Open Images V7 photographs (the training data behind the bundled heads)
  Role: the pictures the eight linear heads were fitted on; no photograph is
    redistributed, only the coefficients fitted from them
  Artifact: 6,604 photographs by 4,951 distinct creators, read once at training
    time from the CVDF mirror of Open Images V7. Creator, profile URL and
    landing page are recorded per image in the training manifests. The
    `frame_kind`, `screen` and `uncovered_person` heads used the partition the
    five older heads were fitted on plus a 2,986-picture top-up
  License: CC BY 2.0, filtered on each row's own licence field
  Copyright: the individual photographers named in the Open Images manifests
  URL: https://storage.googleapis.com/openimages/web/download_v7.html
  Note: no photograph from a private library was used, and this notice does not
    relicense the source photographs.

Laya audience pre-screen (fine-tuned from convaiinnovations/laya-typed-decisions)
  Role: the optional local answer to the audience check's activity question
    (`editorial.laya_audience`, off by default)
  Artifact: laya-audience-a79ad9fa.tar, a bf16 checkpoint of a ModernBERT-large
    encoder with Laya's decision head, fine-tuned by this project, served from the
    `models-v2` release, 811 MB,
    sha256 a79ad9fa3e4b5ae23e6b7ca9233f2bed50746a72baf0c3803dbecd68a6625dc4;
    fetched only by `immich-memories models fetch --laya`
  License: Apache-2.0 (the archive carries LICENSE and NOTICE)
  Copyright: the Laya authors (convaiinnovations, github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya);
    Answer.AI and LightOn (ModernBERT-large)
  URL: https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya-typed-decisions
  Training text: captions written by SmolVLM2-500M for 30,972 public photographs of
    the CommonCatalog CC BY slice of YFCC100M (CC BY 2.0), plus 4,660 synthetic
    captions. Every photographer is credited in ATTRIBUTION.csv inside the archive,
    also published as laya-audience-attribution.csv on the `models-v2` release. No
    photograph is in the archive or relicensed by it. Labels: this project's
    audience question answered by glm-5.3-flash. No picture or caption from any
    user library was used for training.
  Removal: email sam@dropbars.be with the photo id; the photograph is dropped from
    the manifest and from the next checkpoint.
  Runtime: laya-mlx (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/mizorewww/laya-mlx),
    installed separately on Apple silicon
  Portable export: laya-audience-onnx-90420ef3.tar.gz, float32 ONNX,
    sha256 90420ef38a5af3184bfbf9c3d5cdd030f1acac91d6dd911942d11b36e6c07c1a.
    Bundled in the CUDA image with LICENSE, NOTICE and ATTRIBUTION.csv.

SmolVLM2-500M-Video-Instruct (HuggingFaceTB, GGUF export by ggml-org)
  Role: the CUDA image's caption model and image projector
  Artifact: Q8_0 GGUFs at revision ccd7aae53bcb1997355c2f094959e72b3642ce17
    of ggml-org/SmolVLM2-500M-Video-Instruct-GGUF; digests in pinned_models.py
  License: Apache-2.0 (full text also in the bundled Laya LICENSE)
  Copyright: Hugging Face and contributors
  URL: https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/SmolVLM2-500M-Video-Instruct-GGUF

llama.cpp (CUDA caption runtime)
  Role: serves the bundled SmolVLM2 caption model
  Artifact: server-cuda-b10920, revision eafe15a5e3d87dd68ae33acf6a7cbd9415a0ac5e
    image sha256 6b4e57594fbb8fb1111bfe64a470570586bb4649a1d38647680a4ec3ed159695
  License: MIT, reproduced at /opt/llama/LICENSE in the CUDA image
  Copyright: 2023-2026 The ggml authors
  URL: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

Marqo NSFW image detector (Marqo/nsfw-image-detection-384)
  Role: the sensitive-content detector behind the family-viewing gate
  Artifact: nsfw-marqo-384-924658f1.onnx, an ONNX export of revision
    0c26ec22111b83f106d72a55f611ec35962bcb65 written by
    scripts/export_marqo_onnx.py, served from the `models-v1` release, 22 MB,
    sha256 924658f1ac638d96e9126ecb29de047dc8d31c9c9defcab77a26a5c96ed69e11
  License: Apache-2.0
  Copyright: Marqo
  URL: https://huggingface.co/Marqo/nsfw-image-detection-384

Docling document figure classifier (docling-project/DocumentFigureClassifier-v2.0)
  Role: tells a screenshot, a scan or a chart from a photograph
  Artifact: model.onnx at revision 2a12e02668b98ca40216eab41cdf19530577cba4,
    fetched from the Hugging Face Hub into the local cache on first use
  License: Apache-2.0
  Copyright: IBM Corporation (Docling project)
  URL: https://huggingface.co/docling-project/DocumentFigureClassifier-v2.0

YuNet face detector (opencv_zoo)
  Role: the face centre behind smart-zoom framing, on the OpenCV path
  Artifact: face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx at revision
    f12e12798e8314f7c074a6656816c048dcc95b7a, copied byte-for-byte into the
    Python package at src/immich_memories/processing/bundled_models/, 227 KB,
    sha256 8f2383e4dd3cfbb4553ea8718107fc0423210dc964f9f4280604804ed2552fa4
  License: MIT
  Copyright: 2020 Shiqi Yu
  URL: https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/main/models/face_detection_yunet
  Note: opencv_zoo as a whole is Apache-2.0; this model directory carries its
    own MIT LICENSE, and that is the one reproduced here. Bundled rather than
    fetched because it is 227 KB and the machine may never reach the network.

FireRedVAD audio-event detector
  Role: protect speech when selecting and fitting video cut boundaries
  Artifact: fireredvad_aed.onnx, bundled at src/immich_memories/speech/bundled_models/
  License: Apache-2.0; reproduced in bundled_models/LICENSE-FireRedVAD
  URL: https://github.com/FireRedTeam/FireRedVAD

Optional models the app can call but never bundles: a caption model and a text
reader served by the operator (any OpenAI-compatible endpoint), MusicGen
(Meta, CC-BY-NC-4.0 weights) and ACE-Step (Apache-2.0) for generated music,
Demucs (MIT, weights downloaded by the `demucs` package) for stem separation.
Their licences are the operator's to check for the models they choose.


Apache-2.0 notice
-----------------

The three Apache-2.0 models above (YuNet is MIT) are distributed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
Their ONNX exports are derivative works of those checkpoints and carry the
same licence; no NOTICE file accompanies the upstream checkpoints.


Bundled music (packages/immich-memories-music)
----------------------------------------------

28 tracks generated locally with ACE-Step 1.5 (acestep-v15-xl-turbo). Nothing is
sampled from or trained on third-party recordings; the tracks are released under
the project's MIT licence. Model, settings, and per-track tempo, key and seed are
recorded in packages/immich-memories-music/LICENSE-MUSIC.

ACE-Step (the generator, not shipped)
  License: Apache-2.0
  URL: https://github.com/ace-step/ACE-Step


